SECTION 02 // EXECUTIVE INTELLIGENCE SUMMARY
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Immediately following the closure of the spatial conduit above Stark Tower and the neutralizing pulse that severed the Chitauri neural network, S.H.I.E.L.D. mobilized over 1,200 logistical, hazmat, and containment specialists into the greater Midtown Manhattan sector. The mission directive focused on securing a 35-block perimeter, recovering and neutralizing volatile extraterrestrial armaments, preventing civic radiation poisoning, and preempting non-governmental salvage operations.

Under joint executive mandates authorized by Director Nicholas J. Fury and the President of the United States, municipal and private salvage contracts—including local recovery teams led by civilian contractors such as Adrian Toomes—were summarily voided and superseded by federal authority. Custody of primary salvage operations was partitioned between S.H.I.E.L.D. scientific intake teams and the newly chartered executive agency, the United States Department of Damage Control (D.O.D.C.), funded in partnership with Stark Industries.

Recovered material was systematically cataloged, categorized by hazard index, and rerouted to specialized research facilities (primarily Project P.E.G.A.S.U.S. and The Sandbox) or deposited in the D.O.D.C. Deep Vault in upstate New York.

COMMAND ASSESSMENT: Remediation recovered over 91% of estimated alien mass across the primary impact zone. However, urban extraction gaps and municipal jurisdictional friction permitted minor quantities of exotic hardware to bleed into metropolitan organized crime syndicates.

